  "guideIntro": "Check by eye first, then verify each spot with the tools. Below are the most common hiding places — go through them in order.",
  "guideCta": "Found something suspicious? See next steps",
  "guideHow": "How to check: ",
  "guideHint": "Tip: ",
  "guideP1Title": "Smoke detector",
  "guideP1Check": "Stand directly beneath it and look up / from the side; pinholes often hide at metal-plastic seams",
  "guideP1Hint": "Black housings hide pinhole lenses easily — get close and check several angles",
  "guideP2Title": "Outlets & power strips",
  "guideP2Check": "Look for unnatural holes or bulges on the panel; shine a flashlight inside",
  "guideP2Hint": "USB ports, charger holes and power-strip sides are common hiding spots",
  "guideP3Title": "Mirror (two-way)",
  "guideP3Check": "Press a fingernail to the glass: a gap means a normal mirror; no gap means caution",
  "guideP3Hint": "A two-way mirror may hide a room behind it — but the mirror itself can also hold a micro lens",
  "guideP4Title": "Wall art & frames",
  "guideP4Check": "Check the frame edges and the gap behind the painting for extra holes",
  "guideP4Hint": "Hidden compartments behind frames are classic — gently press the frame to feel for oddities",
  "guideP5Title": "AC vents",
  "guideP5Check": "Shine a flashlight into the vent and look for unusual reflections between the fins",
  "guideP5Hint": "The gap above a wall-mounted AC and the wall can hide micro devices",
  "guideP6Title": "Bedside clock / lamp",
  "guideP6Check": "Check the screen, button gaps and base for extra holes",
  "guideP6Hint": "Devices right by the bed are both hidden and close to you — check them first",
  "guideP7Title": "Router / TV box",
  "guideP7Check": "Look for extra LEDs or pinholes beyond the normal lights",
  "guideP7Hint": "Routers are often repurposed as a \"legitimate\" disguise for a camera",
  "guideP8Title": "Plant pots",
  "guideP8Check": "Check the pot and the foliage above the soil for foreign objects",
  "guideP8Hint": "Micro lenses under foliage are hard to spot — combine with the IR scan",
  "guideP9Title": "Lights / smoke detector",
  "guideP9Check": "Check inside lamp shades, chandelier joints and behind bedside wall lamps",
  "guideP9Hint": "Glare near light sources fools the eye — the IR detector is more reliable here",
